    "description": "LBJ Express is the trade name of the managed-lanes concession on I-635 and I-35E in Dallas County, Texas. Its users are commuters, freight carriers, and other motorists seeking priced travel-time reliability through the Dallas-Fort Worth metroplex. The project operates under a long-term toll-concession structure with dynamic pricing, operations and maintenance obligations, and handback requirements at the end of the term. Public disclosures describe a roughly 13-mile corridor with six managed lanes and a total project cost of about $2.6 to $2.7 billion. The road fully opened in 2015 and has since become one of the larger managed-lanes projects in North America. The current project consortium is publicly described as including Cintra, Meridiam, and APG, while current ownership percentages are not publicly disclosed.",
